     _i_n_t
     ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt(_i_n_t _o_f_l_a_g);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() function allocates a new pseudo-terminal and estab‐
     lishes a connection with its master device.  A slave device shall be cre‐
     ated in _/_d_e_v_/_p_t_s.  After the pseudo-terminal has been allocated, the
     slave device should have the proper permissions before it can be used
     (see grantpt(3)).  The name of the slave device can be determined by
     calling ptsname(3).

     The file status flags and file access modes of the open file description
     shall be set according to the value of _o_f_l_a_g.  Values for _o_f_l_a_g are con‐
     structed by a bitwise-inclusive OR of flags from the following list, de‐
     fined in <_f_c_n_t_l_._h>:

     O_RDWR     Open for reading and writing.

     O_NOCTTY   If set ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() shall not cause the terminal device to
                become the controlling terminal for the process.

     O_CLOEXEC  Set the close-on-exec flag for the new file descriptor.

     The ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() function shall fail when _o_f_l_a_g contains other values.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Upon successful completion, the ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() function shall allocate a
     new pseudo-terminal device and return a non-negative integer representing
     a file descriptor, which is connected to its master device.  Otherwise,
     -1 shall be returned and errno set to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() function shall fail if:

     [ENFILE]           The system file table is full.

     [EINVAL]           The value of _o_f_l_a_g is not valid.

     [EAGAIN]           Out of pseudo-terminal resources.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ptsname(3), pts(4), tty(4)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() function conforms to IEEE Std 1003.1-2001 (“POSIX.1”).
     The ability to use O_CLOEXEC is an extension to the standard.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppoossiixx__ooppeennpptt() function appeared in FreeBSD 5.0.  In FreeBSD 8.0,
     this function was changed to a system call.

NNOOTTEESS
     The flag O_NOCTTY is included for compatibility; in FreeBSD, opening a
     terminal does not cause it to become a process's controlling terminal.

